3.Methodology 

3.1 Target Structural Modeling 

Data Sourcing: 

Target sequences from the Comprehensive Antibiotic Resistance Database were retrieved. Focus was on high-priority RND pump MexB (P. aeruginosa) (Du et al., 2015). 

Specific Target Sequences were retrieved manually: 

MexB was searched on the search bar on the CARD Homepage. Once results are seen, specific entry linked to its Antibiotic Resistance Ontology (ARO) classification was selected. Then followed by Scrolling down to the Reference Sequences section on the gene page to view, copy, or download the FASTA-formatted sequences for that specific target. The fasta sequence for the MexB protein was copied. 

Conformational Sampling: 

To robustly train machine learning or molecular docking models against the peristaltic functional cycle of bacterial efflux pumps, it is necessary to gather structural snapshots representing all three asymmetrical functional states: Access/Loose (L), Binding/Tight (T), and Extrusion/Open (O) (Murakami et al., 2006). 

