Residues occurring within 4 Å of a ligand were classified as having a close contact. Aromatic residues showing close contacts were additionally flagged as aromatic-contact candidates. This designation was used as a geometric descriptor and was not interpreted as definitive evidence of a specific π–π interaction (Jerome et al., 2021). 

